From fa2b0fbdb39741159a26686711b5bc3c9c72d5f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 17:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 173/913] clk: stm32mp13: add critical clock flag from common
 clock framework

Prepare the new management of critical clocks by using the
CLK_IS_CRITICAL flag from the common clock framework.

This will allow marking STM32 clocks that must never be disabled.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a5efd5e3ee841aa6e6945e9b203b85bc94651401 clk: stm32mp13: add critical clock flag from common clock framework]
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ie62ca0c71407ff1a26000b0431503af40fae820a
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/545786
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
